examples.solution_text:
Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$:

$\begin{aligned}y&=2^{0}-2\\&=-1.\end{aligned}$

The horizontal asymptote is $y=-2$.

For $x=1$:

$\begin{aligned}y&=2^{1}-2\\&=0.\end{aligned}$

Draw an increasing curve through $(0,-1)$ and $(1,0)$, approaching $y=-2$ on the left.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{asymptotered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,->},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},xmin=-4,xmax=3,ymin=-3,ymax=5,xtick={-3,-2,-1,1,2},ytick={-2,-1,1,2,3,4},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},samples=120,clip=false]
\addplot[asymptotered,dashed,domain=-4:3] {-2};
\node[anchor=north] at (axis cs:1.8,-2) {$y=-2$};
\addplot[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-4:2.7] {exp(x*ln(2))-2};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,curveblue] coordinates {(0,-1) (1,0)};
\node[anchor=west] (interceptlabel) at (axis cs:0.6,-1.25) {$(0,-1)$};
\draw[black,thin,shorten <=2pt,shorten >=2pt] (interceptlabel.west) -- (axis cs:0,-1);
\node[anchor=south east] at (axis cs:1,0.25) {$(1,0)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the $y$-intercept by letting $x=0$:

$\begin{aligned}y&=-2(3^{0})+4\\&=2.\end{aligned}$

The horizontal asymptote is $y=4$.

For $x=1$:

$\begin{aligned}y&=-2(3^{-1})+4\\&=-\frac{2}{3}+4\\&=\frac{10}{3}.\end{aligned}$

The negative exponent reverses the curve horizontally; the negative factor reflects it vertically. Draw an increasing curve through $(0,2)$ and $(1,\frac{10}{3})$, approaching $y=4$ from below on the right.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{asymptotered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,->},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},xmin=-1.5,xmax=4,ymin=-4,ymax=5,xtick={-1,1,2,3},ytick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},samples=120,clip=false]
\addplot[asymptotered,dashed,domain=-1.5:4] {4};
\node[anchor=south] at (axis cs:2.9,4) {$y=4$};
\addplot[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-1.2:4] {-2*exp(-x*ln(3))+4};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,curveblue] coordinates {(0,2) (1,3.333333)};
\node[anchor=east] (interceptlabel) at (axis cs:-0.5,2.3) {$(0,2)$};
\draw[black,thin,shorten <=2pt,shorten >=2pt] (interceptlabel.east) -- (axis cs:0,2);
\node[anchor=north west] (pointlabel) at (axis cs:1.5,2.6) {$(1,\frac{10}{3})$};
\draw[black,thin,shorten <=2pt,shorten >=2pt] (pointlabel.north west) -- (axis cs:1,3.333333);
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

